// Azure Lowkey Vault, comprehensively: re-usable recordings of the Azure Key
// Vault REST API (secrets, keys, certificates) as emulated by Lowkey Vault,
// for any language's tests to replay with no emulator. A "comprehensive"
// suite of servirtium-vcr's pre-recorded/from-testcontainers (the README's
// "Pattern for comprehensive suites"; CouchDB is the pilot). Written for
// servirtium-vcr, not ported from testcontainers-go (whose module test only
// builds a client).
//
// PORTING: this file is the reference for what each tape holds; the tapes
// are the re-usable part. A port is a test in your language and test
// framework that makes the same requests, in the same order, against a
// Servirtium replay server loaded with the tape, and checks the same things.
// Any Servirtium implementation replays them. Every request here is plain
// HTTP/1.1 with these headers and no others:
//   User-Agent: testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)
//   Authorization: Bearer ...     (every case but the first request of the
//                                  login case, see below)
//   Content-Type: application/json (only when there is a body)
// Playback is strict about method, path (query string included, exactly as
// encoded here: ?api-version=7.4 comes first, then any other parameter), the
// recorded request headers and the body (byte for byte: send the JSON bodies
// exactly as written in this file, no spaces), and fails a case whose
// recorded requests are not all made. Host, Connection and Content-Length
// are on the tapes but are transport headers, not compared.
//
// PORTING, the tape for each case: <case>.md beside this file, where <case>
// is the second argument of servirtium.recording(...) in that case. The
// cases are independent: each starts its OWN Lowkey Vault (live) with an
// empty vault, so a list shows exactly what the case made, and any one tape
// replays alone and in any order. (Why not one shared emulator, as CouchDB's
// cases have? A vault has no way to drop its entries: a deleted secret stays
// "deleted but recoverable" and its name cannot be reused or purged, see
// below, so a shared one would make each list depend on the cases that ran
// before.)
//
// HTTPS and the transport
// -----------------------
// Lowkey Vault serves HTTPS on 8443 with a self-signed certificate
// (CN=lowkey-vault.local, SAN includes localhost and 127.0.0.1). When
// recording, the test talks plain HTTP to the recorder, which talks HTTPS to
// the container and verifies it against that certificate
// (servirtium.trust_upstream_ca; the PEM is read from the container with
// `openssl s_client`, so recording needs the openssl command-line tool). TLS
// is the connection's business, so nothing about it is on the tape, and
// playback is plain HTTP. A port replays over HTTP: an Azure SDK client has
// to be told to allow a non-TLS endpoint and to skip its challenge-based
// authentication's HTTPS requirement (azure-sdk "disable challenge resource
// verification" / "allow insecure"), or the port tests with raw HTTP as here.
// The `id`, `kid`, `recoveryId` and `nextLink` URLs in a response name the
// vault as https://<host:port>; the tapes carry {{request.host}} there, which
// playback fills with the replay server's own host and port (still with
// an https scheme: build follow-up requests from the PATH of such a URL, as
// these cases do, not from the URL).
//
// Login, and "already logged in"
// ------------------------------
// Lowkey Vault does not check tokens. Any `Authorization: Bearer <anything>`
// is accepted, and a request with no Authorization is answered 401 with
//   WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource="https://<host>", authorization_uri="https://<host>/<path>"
// which is the Key Vault challenge an Azure client reads to learn what token
// to ask for. The token source is the managed-identity simulation on the
// metadata port (8080): GET /metadata/identity/oauth2/token?api-version=
// 2019-08-01&resource=<resource> with an X-IDENTITY-HEADER: header answers a
// JWT-shaped access_token (and refresh_token) with a one-hour expiry.
//
// Logging in gets its own tapes, two because the token comes from a second
// port of the container (as Azurite's first case does for blob and queue):
//   challenges_and_gets_a_token_from_the_identity_endpoint          the vault port: the 401 challenge, then
//                                                                   a request with the token, then one with
//                                                                   an invented token (accepted too)
//   challenges_and_gets_a_token_from_the_identity_endpoint_identity the metadata port: the token request
// Every other case is ALREADY LOGGED IN: each request carries
//   Authorization: Bearer <token>
// (when recording, the token is fetched live from the identity endpoint,
// outside the recorder, before the case starts) and the tapes hold it as
// `Authorization: Bearer AUTHORIZATION_1` (Servirtium's redact_credentials
// preset), which playback matches on PRESENCE, not value.
//
// PORTING, getting into the logged-in state without the login tapes: send
// any `Authorization: Bearer <anything>` header on every request. A
// consequence of presence matching: a replay cannot tell a valid token from
// an invented one (and neither can Lowkey Vault), so the unauthorized case
// sends no Authorization header at all. The identity request's
// X-IDENTITY-HEADER (the emulator's fixed "header") is redacted the same
// way, as X_IDENTITY_HEADER_1 (redact_credential_header).
//
// What varies between runs, and what the tapes do with it
// --------------------------------------------------------
// Every rule is registered in api_rules() below, with its reason; the
// "## [Recording rules]" table at the end of each tape lists them all and
// the interactions each touched ("none" where it did not). In short:
//   - normalized (each distinct value a stable {{name-N}} token, the same
//     token wherever it recurs, because a client sends it back): the
//     32-hex version ids ({{version-N}}: in every `id`/`kid`, in the paths
//     of the version-specific requests, in error messages, and a pending
//     certificate's request_id), and the signature, wrapped key and
//     ciphertext blobs ({{blob-N}}: a client sends each back to verify,
//     unwrap or decrypt), and the access and refresh JWTs ({{jwt-N}}).
//   - collapsed (one constant; nobody sends them back): attribute times
//     (created, updated, deletedDate, scheduledPurgeDate, and a
//     certificate's own exp and nbf), the RSA modulus and EC coordinates of
//     a generated key, a certificate's DER (cer), signing request (csr) and
//     thumbprint (x5t), the identity token's expires_on, and the
//     timestamp in Spring's generic error bodies.
//   - redacted: the Authorization bearer token and X-IDENTITY-HEADER
//     (credential presets, matched on presence).
//   - left out: the Date response header, as everywhere, and Allow (the
//     methods of a 405 in a varying order).
//   Deterministic values are left alone, on purpose: a secret's value,
//   contentType and tags, `recoverableDays` (90) and `recoveryLevel`
//   ("Recoverable"), a client-chosen `exp` on a secret, a key's public
//   exponent (AQAB) and `key_ops`, a certificate's policy.
//   (Time fields on certificates are collapsed with a pattern that needs
//   exp and nbf together; the secrets here set only `exp`, never both.)
//
// PORTING: in playback, a normalized or redacted value comes back as its
// token, verbatim: a version is "{{version-1}}", a signature "{{blob-1}}",
// the bearer AUTHORIZATION_1. Treat every id and blob as an opaque string
// (never assert its length or shape) and send it back exactly as received;
// the tape expects the token in the later request, e.g. `GET
// /secrets/tcae-secret/{{version-1}}?api-version=7.4`. Send the braces as
// they are. A response's JSON key order and the order of lists are what
// Lowkey Vault produces: keys alphabetical, lists of entities by name. A
// list of the VERSIONS of one name is NOT in creation order: it is ordered by
// the version id, which is random, so two or more versions would come back in
// a different order on every run and the tape would differ between records.
// The cases therefore list the versions of a name only while it has ONE, and
// read the later versions by id or as "latest" (which is the newest by
// creation time, in whole seconds: the cases wait a second between writes to
// one name so that cannot be a clock tie). Servirtium writing a stable order
// would lift this (servirtium-vcr TODO.md).
//
// In and out of scope
// -------------------
// In: secrets (set, get latest and by version, versions, list, paging with
// maxresults and the $skiptoken of nextLink, update of attributes and tags
// on one version, delete, deleted list/get, recover, a refused purge); keys
// (create RSA and EC, a second version, get latest and by version, versions,
// list, update key_ops, sign / verify, wrapKey / unwrapKey, encrypt /
// decrypt, delete, recover, rotate); certificates (create with a self-signed policy,
// the pending operation, get latest and by version, versions, list, policy,
// delete, recover); the challenge and the token; and the representative
// errors 400, 401, 404, 405, 409 and 500 (Lowkey Vault answers several
// client mistakes with 500 or a bare 404, and the tapes keep what it does).
// Out: purge that succeeds (a purgeable vault has to be created through the
// management API under a different host name, and the recorder forwards one
// Host; this default vault is Recoverable and refuses), backup / restore
// (the blob is a gzip of times and keys), certificate import and issuers and
// contacts and operations other than the pending read, managed HSM, key
// import, vaults other than the
// default and the management API, and the Azure SDKs' own flows (these are
// the raw REST calls they make). Each could be a later case.
//
// Running it (from pre-recorded/from-testcontainers):
//   ae test lowkeyvault/test_lowkeyvault.ae                     container, no Servirtium
//   TCAE_VCR=record   ae test lowkeyvault/test_lowkeyvault.ae   write the tapes
//   TCAE_VCR=check    ae test lowkeyvault/test_lowkeyvault.ae   fail if a tape changed
//   TCAE_VCR=playback ae test lowkeyvault/test_lowkeyvault.ae   no container: the tapes
// Recording needs the openssl command-line tool on the PATH.

import std.spec
import std.string
import std.fs
import std.os
import std.json
import std.list
import std.http.client
import testcontainers as tc
import testcontainers.docker
import testcontainers.testing
import servirtium
import modules.azure.lowkeyvault

const IMAGE = "nagyesta/lowkey-vault:7.3.48-ubi10-minimal"

// The User-Agent this test's HTTP client sends, as an app's client library
// would (Aether's std.http.client adds none). Servirtium records what the
// client sends and adds nothing of its own.
const USER_AGENT = "testcontainers-ae-tests (Aether std.http.client)"

// The query every request carries.
const V = "api-version=7.4"

// The bearer token the logged-in cases send in playback, where there is no
// emulator to ask. Any value does: the tapes match the header on presence.
const PLAYBACK_TOKEN = "any-value-replay-matches-on-presence"

// The resource a token is asked for, as an Azure client does for Key Vault.
const RESOURCE = "https%3A%2F%2Fvault.azure.net"

// SHA-256 of "hello", base64url without padding: the digest the key cases
// sign, and (32 bytes) the key material they wrap.
const DIGEST = "LPJNul-wow4m6DsqxbninhsWHlwfp0JecwQzYpOLmCQ"

// SHA-256 of "world": another 32-byte digest, which the signature made over
// DIGEST does not fit.
const OTHER_DIGEST = "SG6kYiTRu0-2gPNPfJrZao8k7Ii-c-qOWmxlJg6cuKc"

// "hello", base64url: the plaintext the encrypt cases use.
const PLAINTEXT = "aGVsbG8"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// HTTP helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The WWW-Authenticate header of the last response (the challenge).
var last_www_authenticate: string = ""

// One second between two writes to the same name, live only, so their
// created times (seconds) differ and a version list's order cannot depend on
// a clock tie.
fn pause() {
    if servirtium.live() == 1 { sleep(1100) }
}

// One HTTP request: (status, body, error). hdrs are "Name: value" lines;
// ctype is the body's Content-Type (none when the body is empty). An https
// URL is verified against `cafile` when it is set.
fn http_send(method: string, url: string, hdrs: string[], ctype: string, body: string, cafile: string) -> (int, string, string) {
    req = client.request(method, url)
    client.set_header(req, "User-Agent", USER_AGENT)
    client.set_timeout(req, 60s)
    if string.length(cafile) > 0 && string.starts_with(url, "https:") == 1 {
        cerr = client.set_cafile(req, cafile)
        if cerr != "" { return 0, "", cerr }
    }
    for h in hdrs {
        colon = string.index_of(h, ":")
        client.set_header(req, string.substring(h, 0, colon), string.trim(string.substring(h, colon + 1, string.length(h))))
    }
    if string.length(body) > 0 { client.set_body(req, string.bytes(body), ctype) }
    r, err = client.send_request(req)
    client.request_free(req)
    if err != "" { return 0, "", err }
    st = client.response_status(r)
    b = client.response_body(r)
    last_www_authenticate = client.response_header(r, "WWW-Authenticate")
    client.response_free(r)
    return st, b, ""
}


// The current case's vault: the base URL of the recording, the PEM the https
// container is verified against (only when a recording is off, i.e. direct),
// and the bearer token every logged-in request carries.
var api: string = ""
var cafile: string = ""
var token: string = ""

// A logged-in request with a JSON body (or none): (status, body). A
// transport error fails the case.
fn kv(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}${path}", ["Authorization: Bearer ${token}"], "application/json", body, cafile)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// A request with no credentials at all: (status, body).
fn anonymous(method: string, path: string, body: string) -> (int, string) {
    st, b, err = http_send(method, "${api}${path}", [], "application/json", body, cafile)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "${method} ${path}")
    return st, b
}

// String equality (Aether's == on strings compares identity).
fn same(a: string, b: string) -> bool {
    return string.equals(a, b) == 1
}

// A string in a JSON body by a dotted path ("id", "key.kid", "value.0.id");
// "" when absent or not a string.
fn jstr(body: string, path: string) -> string {
    doc, err = json.parse(body)
    if err != "" { return "" }
    let v: ptr = doc
    rest = path
    while string.length(rest) > 0 && v != null {
        p = rest
        dot = string.index_of(rest, ".")
        if dot >= 0 {
            p = string.substring(rest, 0, dot)
            rest = string.substring(rest, dot + 1, string.length(rest))
        } else {
            rest = ""
        }
        if json.json_type(v) == json.JSON_ARRAY {
            idx, _ = string.to_int(p)
            a, _ = json.array_get(v, idx)
            v = a
        } else {
            o, _ = json.object_get(v, p)
            v = o
        }
    }
    out = ""
    if v != null {
        s, serr = json.get_string(v)
        if serr == "" { out = string.copy(s) }
    }
    json.free(doc)
    return out
}

// The version (last path segment) of an id URL such as
// https://host/secrets/name/<version>: "{{version-1}}" on replay.
fn version_of(id_url: string) -> string {
    i = string.length(id_url) - 1
    while i >= 0 {
        if same(string.substring(id_url, i, i + 1), "/") { return string.substring(id_url, i + 1, string.length(id_url)) }
        i = i - 1
    }
    return ""
}

// The path (from the first / after the authority) of an id URL.
fn path_of(url: string) -> string {
    start = string.index_of(url, "://")
    if start < 0 { return url }
    rest = string.substring(url, start + 3, string.length(url))
    slash = string.index_of(rest, "/")
    if slash < 0 { return "/" }
    return string.substring(rest, slash, string.length(rest))
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The live emulator of the current case (record, check and off modes only)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

// The PEM of the certificate `authority` (host:port) serves, read with the
// openssl command-line tool: "" and an error when it cannot.
fn server_cert_pem(authority: string) -> (string, string) {
    argv = list.new()
    for a in ["s_client", "-connect", authority, "-servername", "localhost"] { list.add(argv, a) }
    out, _e, rc, err = os.run_full("openssl", argv, null, "")
    list.free(argv)
    if err != "" { return "", "openssl: ${err}" }
    begin_at = string.index_of(out, "-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----")
    end_marker = "-----END CERTIFICATE-----"
    end_at = string.index_of(out, end_marker)
    if begin_at < 0 || end_at < 0 { return "", "openssl s_client printed no certificate (rc ${rc})" }
    return string.concat(string.substring(out, begin_at, end_at + string.length(end_marker)), "\n"), ""
}

// Start a vault for the case, and ask it for a token. Live modes only.
// Returns the vault's base URL ("" on failure); sets `token`, and
// `cafile_live` to a PEM file of its certificate. `meta` is the metadata
// port's base URL.
var cafile_live: string = ""
var meta_live: string = ""

fn start_vault() -> string {
    c, err = lowkeyvault.run(IMAGE)
    if c == null {
        spec.fail("lowkey vault starts: ${err}")
        return ""
    }
    testing.cleanup_container(c)
    spec.assert_ok(err, "lowkey vault starts")
    if err != "" { return "" }
    auth, aerr = lowkeyvault.host_authority(c, lowkeyvault.API_PORT, lowkeyvault.LOCAL)
    spec.assert_ok(aerr, "the vault's host:port")
    mauth, merr = lowkeyvault.host_authority(c, lowkeyvault.METADATA_PORT, lowkeyvault.LOCAL)
    spec.assert_ok(merr, "the metadata port's host:port")
    if aerr != "" || merr != "" { return "" }
    pem, perr = server_cert_pem(auth)
    spec.assert_ok(perr, "read the vault's certificate")
    if perr != "" { return "" }
    dir, derr = fs.make_temp_dir("", "tcae-lowkey-")
    spec.assert_ok(derr, "temp dir")
    cafile_live = "${dir}/lowkey-vault.pem"
    fs.write(cafile_live, pem)
    servirtium.trust_upstream_ca(cafile_live)
    meta_live = "http://${mauth}"
    return "https://${auth}"
}

// An access token from the identity endpoint, outside any recording.
fn token_live() -> string {
    st, b, err = http_send("GET", "${meta_live}/metadata/identity/oauth2/token?api-version=2019-08-01&resource=${RESOURCE}", ["X-IDENTITY-HEADER: ${lowkeyvault.identity_header()}"], "", "", "")
    spec.assert_ok(err, "get a token (not recorded)")
    spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get a token (not recorded): ${b}")
    return jstr(b, "access_token")
}

// Remove the temporary PEM and forget the trust.
fn end_vault() {
    servirtium.trust_upstream_ca("")
    if string.length(cafile_live) > 0 {
        fs.delete(cafile_live)
        cafile_live = ""
    }
}

// Start a logged-in case: in a live mode, a fresh vault and a token (neither
// recorded); then the recording. Sets `api`, `cafile` and `token`; returns
// the recording handle, and ok = 0 when the case cannot run.
fn begin(case_: string) -> (ptr, int) {
    addr = ""
    token = PLAYBACK_TOKEN
    cafile = ""
    if servirtium.live() == 1 {
        addr = start_vault()
        if addr == "" { return null, 0 }
        token = token_live()
        // Off mode talks to the container directly over https; a recording's
        // base is plain http, to which the PEM does not apply.
        cafile = cafile_live
    }
    base, rec = servirtium.recording("lowkeyvault", case_, addr)
    api = base
    return rec, 1
}

// Finish a case: end the recording and drop the certificate file.
fn finish(rec: ptr) {
    servirtium.end_recording(rec)
    end_vault()
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Recording rules
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

fn api_rules() {
    servirtium.clear_rules()
    // Lowkey Vault is MIT-licensed: no licence notice is needed.

    // The bearer token on every logged-in request: Servirtium's credential
    // preset writes it as AUTHORIZATION_N and replays the header on presence.
    servirtium.redact_credentials()
    // The managed-identity request's own header (the emulator's fixed
    // "header"): the same treatment, so no credential is on any tape.
    servirtium.redact_credential_header("X-IDENTITY-HEADER")

    // Version ids: 32 lower-case hex after a "/" or a quote and before a "/",
    // a quote or a "?": in `id`/`kid` URLs, in the path of a version-specific
    // request, in error messages, and a pending certificate's request_id.
    // Normalized, not collapsed: a client sends a version back in a path.
    servirtium.normalize("(?<=[/\"])[0-9a-f]{32}(?=[/\"?])", "version")
    // The blobs a client sends back: a signature (to verify), a wrapped key
    // (to unwrap) and a ciphertext (to decrypt), each one `"value":"<base64url>"`
    // of 80+ characters (a 2048-bit RSA result is 342, an ES256 signature
    // 86). Secret values and the digests the cases send (43) are shorter and
    // stay. RSA padding and ECDSA's nonce are random, so the same input gives
    // a different blob every run.
    servirtium.normalize("(?<=\"value\":\")[A-Za-z0-9_-]{80,}(?=\")", "blob")
    // A 405's Allow header lists the methods in a Java set's order, which
    // differs between runs ("PUT, DELETE, GET" or "PUT, GET, DELETE").
    servirtium.remove_header(servirtium.FIELD_RESPONSE_HEADERS, "Allow")
    // The identity endpoint's JWTs (access_token and refresh_token are the
    // same string): header.payload.signature, the payload carrying issue and
    // expiry times and the signature a fresh value. A client sends the access
    // token back as the bearer, so it is normalized rather than collapsed.
    servirtium.normalize("eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+", "jwt")
    // The token's absolute expiry.
    servirtium.collapse("\"expires_on\":[0-9]+", "\"expires_on\":946684800")

    // Attribute times (Unix seconds): when an entity was created, updated and
    // deleted, and when a deleted one would be purged (deleted + 90 days).
    // Nobody sends them back.
    servirtium.collapse("\"created\":[0-9]{10}", "\"created\":946684800")
    servirtium.collapse("\"updated\":[0-9]{10}", "\"updated\":946684800")
    servirtium.collapse("\"deletedDate\":[0-9]{10}", "\"deletedDate\":946684800")
    servirtium.collapse("\"scheduledPurgeDate\":[0-9]{10}", "\"scheduledPurgeDate\":954460800")
    // A certificate's validity window starts when it was made and lasts
    // validity_months, so both ends move. They are the only attributes with
    // exp AND nbf side by side (the secrets in this suite set `exp` alone).
    servirtium.collapse("\"exp\":[0-9]{10},\"nbf\":[0-9]{10}", "\"exp\":978307200,\"nbf\":946684800")
    // A generated key's public parts: the RSA modulus and an EC point.
    // Different on every run, never sent back (a client verifies with the key
    // id). The exponent "AQAB" and the curve are stable and stay.
    servirtium.collapse("\"n\":\"[A-Za-z0-9_-]{300,}\"", "\"n\":\"RSA-MODULUS\"")
    servirtium.collapse("\"x\":\"[A-Za-z0-9_-]{40,}\"", "\"x\":\"EC-X\"")
    servirtium.collapse("\"y\":\"[A-Za-z0-9_-]{40,}\"", "\"y\":\"EC-Y\"")
    // A certificate's DER, its signing request and its SHA-1 thumbprint,
    // all derived from a generated key.
    servirtium.collapse("\"cer\":\"[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+\"", "\"cer\":\"CERTIFICATE-DER\"")
    servirtium.collapse("\"csr\":\"[A-Za-z0-9+/=]+\"", "\"csr\":\"CERTIFICATE-REQUEST\"")
    servirtium.collapse("\"x5t\":\"[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\"", "\"x5t\":\"THUMBPRINT\"")
    // Spring's generic error body (a 400, 405 or 500 the application did not
    // shape) carries the time of the failure.
    servirtium.collapse("\"timestamp\":\"[^\"]+\"", "\"timestamp\":\"2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\"")
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

main() {
    fw = spec.init()
    if servirtium.skip_if_no_engine(fw) == 1 { return spec.run_summary(fw) }

    api_rules()
    spec.describe(fw, "Azure Key Vault API (Lowkey Vault)") {
        spec.after_each() callback { testing.cleanup_all() }

        // ---- the login tapes -----------------------------------------------

        // PORTING: two tapes. The metadata port first (the token):
        //   challenges_and_gets_a_token_from_the_identity_endpoint_identity.md
        //   GET /metadata/identity/oauth2/token?api-version=2019-08-01&resource=https%3A%2F%2Fvault.azure.net
        //       X-IDENTITY-HEADER: X_IDENTITY_HEADER_1   (the emulator's "header", on presence)
        //       -> 200 {"resource":"https://vault.azure.net","access_token":"{{jwt-1}}","refresh_token":"{{jwt-1}}",
        //               "expires_in":3600,"expires_on":946684800,"token_type":"Bearer"}
        //          (and a WWW-Authenticate: Basic realm=assumed-identity header)
        // then the vault port:
        //   challenges_and_gets_a_token_from_the_identity_endpoint.md
        //   GET /secrets/tcae-login?api-version=7.4        no Authorization
        //       -> 401, an empty body, WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource="https://{{request.host}}", authorization_uri="https://{{request.host}}/secrets/tcae-login"
        //   GET /secrets?api-version=7.4   Authorization: Bearer <the access_token>
        //       -> 200 {"value":[]}   (an empty vault)
        //   GET /secrets?api-version=7.4   Authorization: Bearer an-invented-token
        //       -> 200, the same: the emulator does not check a token
        // The bearer is on the tape as AUTHORIZATION_1 and AUTHORIZATION_2:
        // playback matches the header on presence, so any value passes.
        spec.it("answers a request without a token with a challenge, and takes a token from the identity endpoint") callback {
            addr = ""
            maddr = ""
            cafile = ""
            if servirtium.live() == 1 {
                addr = start_vault()
                if addr == "" { return }
                maddr = meta_live
                cafile = cafile_live
            }
            // 1. the token, from the metadata port
            mbase, mrec = servirtium.recording("lowkeyvault", "challenges_and_gets_a_token_from_the_identity_endpoint_identity", maddr)
            st, b, err = http_send("GET", "${mbase}/metadata/identity/oauth2/token?api-version=2019-08-01&resource=${RESOURCE}", ["X-IDENTITY-HEADER: ${lowkeyvault.identity_header()}"], "", "", "")
            spec.assert_ok(err, "GET the identity token")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "a token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"token_type\":\"Bearer\"", "a bearer token")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"expires_in\":3600", "valid for an hour")
            got = jstr(b, "access_token")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(got) > 0, "an access_token")
            servirtium.end_recording(mrec)

            // 2. the vault port: the challenge, then the token, then any token
            base, rec = servirtium.recording("lowkeyvault", "challenges_and_gets_a_token_from_the_identity_endpoint", addr)
            api = base
            st, b = anonymous("GET", "/secrets/tcae-login?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 401, "no token: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(last_www_authenticate, "Bearer resource=\"https://", "the challenge names the resource")
            spec.assert_contains(last_www_authenticate, "authorization_uri=", "and where to get a token")
            token = got
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the token is accepted: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"value\":[]}", "an empty vault")
            token = "an-invented-token"
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "any token is accepted: ${b}")
            finish(rec)
        }

        // ---- already logged in from here on: every request carries the token

        // PORTING (name tcae-secret; 1 s pause between the writes):
        //   PUT   /secrets/tcae-secret?api-version=7.4 {"value":"first"} -> 200, id https://{{request.host}}/secrets/tcae-secret/{{version-1}}, value "first"
        //   PUT   /secrets/tcae-secret?api-version=7.4 {"value":"second","contentType":"text/plain","tags":{"purpose":"test"},"attributes":{"exp":1900000000}}
        //         -> 200, a new version ({{version-2}}), contentType, tags, attributes.exp 1900000000
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-secret?api-version=7.4                -> 200, the latest: value "second"
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-secret/{{version-1}}?api-version=7.4  -> 200, value "first"
        //   PATCH /secrets/tcae-secret/{{version-2}}?api-version=7.4 {"tags":{"purpose":"patched"},"attributes":{"enabled":false}} -> 200 (no value)
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-secret?api-version=7.4                -> 404 "Operation get is not allowed on a disabled entity." (the latest version is disabled)
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-secret/{{version-1}}?api-version=7.4  -> 200, still readable
        //   PUT   /secrets/tcae-secret-b?api-version=7.4 {"value":"b"} -> 200
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-secret-b/versions?api-version=7.4     -> 200, {"value":[{..one entry..}]} (a list never carries values; see the header on why one version only)
        //   GET   /secrets?api-version=7.4&maxresults=1               -> 200, one entry (tcae-secret) and a nextLink
        //         https://{{request.host}}/secrets?api-version=7.4&$skiptoken=1&maxresults=1
        //   GET   /secrets?api-version=7.4&$skiptoken=1&maxresults=1  -> 200, tcae-secret-b, no nextLink (the path and query of the nextLink)
        // Attribute times, value-less lists: see the header.
        spec.it("sets, reads, versions, updates and lists secrets") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("sets_reads_versions_updates_and_lists_secrets")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = kv("PUT", "/secrets/tcae-secret?${V}", "{\"value\":\"first\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "set: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"value\":\"first\"", "the value")
            v1 = version_of(jstr(b, "id"))
            spec.assert_true(string.length(v1) > 0, "a version id")
            pause()
            st, b = kv("PUT", "/secrets/tcae-secret?${V}", "{\"value\":\"second\",\"contentType\":\"text/plain\",\"tags\":{\"purpose\":\"test\"},\"attributes\":{\"exp\":1900000000}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "set a new version: ${b}")
            v2 = version_of(jstr(b, "id"))
            spec.assert_true(!same(v2, v1), "a different version")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"contentType\":\"text/plain\"", "content type")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"exp\":1900000000", "expiry")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"tags\":{\"purpose\":\"test\"}", "tags")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-secret?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get the latest: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"value\":\"second\"", "the latest value")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-secret/${v1}?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get the first version: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"value\":\"first\"", "the first value")
            st, b = kv("PATCH", "/secrets/tcae-secret/${v2}?${V}", "{\"tags\":{\"purpose\":\"patched\"},\"attributes\":{\"enabled\":false}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "update the second version: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"enabled\":false", "disabled")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"purpose\":\"patched\"", "retagged")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-secret?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "the disabled latest version is not readable: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Operation get is not allowed on a disabled entity.", "disabled")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-secret/${v1}?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the first version still is: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("PUT", "/secrets/tcae-secret-b?${V}", "{\"value\":\"b\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "a second secret: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-secret-b/versions?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "versions of a one-version secret: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(jstr(b, "value.0.id")) > 0, "one entry")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "value.1.id"), "", "and no second")
            spec.assert_true(string.index_of(b, "\"value\":\"b\"") < 0, "a list carries no secret value")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets?${V}&maxresults=1", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the first page: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/secrets/tcae-secret\"", "tcae-secret first, by name")
            next = jstr(b, "nextLink")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(next) > 0, "a nextLink")
            st, b = kv("GET", path_of(next), "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the second page: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/secrets/tcae-secret-b\"", "tcae-secret-b")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "nextLink"), "", "no third page")
            finish(rec)
        }

        // PORTING (name tcae-del):
        //   PUT    /secrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4 {"value":"gone soon"} -> 200
        //   DELETE /secrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4  -> 200, the secret with deletedDate, recoveryId https://{{request.host}}/deletedsecrets/tcae-del, scheduledPurgeDate
        //   GET    /secrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4  -> 404 NotFoundException
        //   GET    /deletedsecrets?api-version=7.4    -> 200, one entry (no value)
        //   GET    /deletedsecrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4 -> 200, with the value
        //   PUT    /secrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4 {"value":"again"} -> 409 AlreadyExistsException: a deleted entity already exists with this name
        //   POST   /deletedsecrets/tcae-del/recover?api-version=7.4 -> 200, the secret again
        //   GET    /secrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4  -> 200 "gone soon"
        //   DELETE /secrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4  -> 200
        //   DELETE /deletedsecrets/tcae-del?api-version=7.4 -> 500 IllegalStateException "The selected elements cannot be purged." (this vault is Recoverable)
        //   POST   /deletedsecrets/tcae-del/recover?api-version=7.4 -> 200
        //   DELETE /secrets/tcae-missing?api-version=7.4 -> 404
        //   POST   /deletedsecrets/tcae-missing/recover?api-version=7.4 -> 404
        spec.it("deletes, lists the deleted, recovers and fails to purge a secret") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("deletes_recovers_and_fails_to_purge_a_secret")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = kv("PUT", "/secrets/tcae-del?${V}", "{\"value\":\"gone soon\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "set: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/secrets/tcae-del?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"deletedDate\":", "deletedDate")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/deletedsecrets/tcae-del\"", "recoveryId")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-del?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a deleted secret is not found: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "NotFoundException", "not found")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/deletedsecrets?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "deleted list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/secrets/tcae-del\"", "listed as deleted")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/deletedsecrets/tcae-del?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get a deleted secret: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"value\":\"gone soon\"", "its value is still there")
            st, b = kv("PUT", "/secrets/tcae-del?${V}", "{\"value\":\"again\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 409, "the name is taken by the deleted one: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "A deleted entity already exists with this name", "already exists")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/deletedsecrets/tcae-del/recover?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "recover: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-del?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "it is back: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"value\":\"gone soon\"", "with its value")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/secrets/tcae-del?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete again: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/deletedsecrets/tcae-del?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "purge is refused: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "The selected elements cannot be purged.", "cannot be purged")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/deletedsecrets/tcae-del/recover?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "recover again: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/secrets/tcae-missing?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "delete a missing secret: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/deletedsecrets/tcae-missing/recover?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "recover a missing secret: ${b}")
            finish(rec)
        }

        // PORTING (names tcae-rsa, tcae-ec; 1 s pause between the two creates of tcae-rsa):
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/create?api-version=7.4 {"kty":"RSA","key_size":2048,"key_ops":["sign","verify","wrapKey","unwrapKey","encrypt","decrypt"],"tags":{"purpose":"test"}}
        //         -> 200 {"attributes":{..},"key":{"e":"AQAB","key_ops":[..],"kid":"https://{{request.host}}/keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}","kty":"RSA","n":"RSA-MODULUS"},"tags":{"purpose":"test"}}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/create?api-version=7.4 (same body) -> 200, a second version
        //   GET   /keys/tcae-rsa?api-version=7.4                    -> 200, the latest ({{version-2}})
        //   GET   /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}?api-version=7.4      -> 200
        //   GET   /keys?api-version=7.4                             -> 200, tcae-ec and tcae-rsa by name
        //   GET   /keys/tcae-ec/versions?api-version=7.4            -> 200, one entry, no key material
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}/sign?api-version=7.4   {"alg":"RS256","value":"<DIGEST>"} -> 200 {"kid":..,"value":"{{blob-1}}"}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}/verify?api-version=7.4 {"alg":"RS256","digest":"<DIGEST>","value":"{{blob-1}}"} -> 200 {"value":true}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}/verify?api-version=7.4 {"alg":"RS256","digest":"SG6kYiTRu0-2gPNPfJrZao8k7Ii-c-qOWmxlJg6cuKc","value":"{{blob-1}}"} -> 200 {"value":false}  (the digest of "world")
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}/wrapkey?api-version=7.4   {"alg":"RSA-OAEP","value":"<DIGEST>"} -> 200 {"kid":..,"value":"{{blob-2}}"}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}/unwrapkey?api-version=7.4 {"alg":"RSA-OAEP","value":"{{blob-2}}"} -> 200 {"kid":..,"value":"<DIGEST>"}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}/encrypt?api-version=7.4   {"alg":"RSA-OAEP-256","value":"aGVsbG8"} -> 200 {"kid":..,"value":"{{blob-3}}"}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-rsa/{{version-1}}/decrypt?api-version=7.4   {"alg":"RSA-OAEP-256","value":"{{blob-3}}"} -> 200 {"kid":..,"value":"aGVsbG8"}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-ec/create?api-version=7.4 {"kty":"EC","crv":"P-256","key_ops":["sign","verify"]} -> 200, "x":"EC-X","y":"EC-Y"
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-ec/{{version-3}}/sign?api-version=7.4   {"alg":"ES256","value":"<DIGEST>"} -> 200 {"value":"{{blob-4}}"}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-ec/{{version-3}}/verify?api-version=7.4 {"alg":"ES256","digest":"<DIGEST>","value":"{{blob-4}}"} -> 200 {"value":true}
        // The version a request names is the version of the key in the response
        // that made it; the tokens are numbered in order of first appearance.
        spec.it("creates RSA and EC keys, signs, verifies, wraps, encrypts and lists versions") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_keys_and_signs_verifies_wraps_and_encrypts")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            rsa = "{\"kty\":\"RSA\",\"key_size\":2048,\"key_ops\":[\"sign\",\"verify\",\"wrapKey\",\"unwrapKey\",\"encrypt\",\"decrypt\"],\"tags\":{\"purpose\":\"test\"}}"
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/create?${V}", rsa)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create an RSA key: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"kty\":\"RSA\"", "RSA")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"e\":\"AQAB\"", "the public exponent")
            v1 = version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid"))
            spec.assert_true(string.length(v1) > 0, "a key version")
            pause()
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/create?${V}", rsa)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create it again: ${b}")
            v2 = version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid"))
            spec.assert_true(!same(v2, v1), "a second version")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys/tcae-rsa?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get the latest: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(same(version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid")), v2), "the second version")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get the first version: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(same(version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid")), v1), "the first version")

            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}/sign?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RS256\",\"value\":\"${DIGEST}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "sign: ${b}")
            sig = jstr(b, "value")
            spec.assert_true(string.length(sig) > 0, "a signature")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}/verify?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RS256\",\"digest\":\"${DIGEST}\",\"value\":\"${sig}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "verify: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"value\":true}", "the signature is good")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}/verify?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RS256\",\"digest\":\"${OTHER_DIGEST}\",\"value\":\"${sig}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "verify against another digest: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"value\":false}", "the signature does not fit it")

            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}/wrapkey?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RSA-OAEP\",\"value\":\"${DIGEST}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "wrap a key: ${b}")
            wrapped = jstr(b, "value")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}/unwrapkey?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RSA-OAEP\",\"value\":\"${wrapped}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "unwrap it: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "value"), DIGEST, "the key that went in comes out")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}/encrypt?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RSA-OAEP-256\",\"value\":\"${PLAINTEXT}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "encrypt: ${b}")
            cipher = jstr(b, "value")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-rsa/${v1}/decrypt?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RSA-OAEP-256\",\"value\":\"${cipher}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "decrypt: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(jstr(b, "value"), PLAINTEXT, "the plaintext comes back")

            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-ec/create?${V}", "{\"kty\":\"EC\",\"crv\":\"P-256\",\"key_ops\":[\"sign\",\"verify\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create an EC key: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"crv\":\"P-256\"", "P-256")
            ev = version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid"))
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-ec/${ev}/sign?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"ES256\",\"value\":\"${DIGEST}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "sign with EC: ${b}")
            esig = jstr(b, "value")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-ec/${ev}/verify?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"ES256\",\"digest\":\"${DIGEST}\",\"value\":\"${esig}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "verify with EC: ${b}")
            spec.assert_str_eq(b, "{\"value\":true}", "the EC signature is good")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/keys/tcae-ec\"", "tcae-ec")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/keys/tcae-rsa\"", "tcae-rsa")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys/tcae-ec/versions?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "versions of a one-version key: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(same(version_of(jstr(b, "value.0.kid")), ev), "its only version")
            spec.assert_true(string.index_of(b, "\"kty\"") < 0, "no key material in a list")
            finish(rec)
        }

        // PORTING (name tcae-key; 1 s pause before the rotate):
        //   POST   /keys/tcae-key/create?api-version=7.4 {"kty":"RSA","key_size":2048,"key_ops":["sign","verify","encrypt","decrypt","wrapKey","unwrapKey"]} -> 200
        //   PATCH  /keys/tcae-key/{{version-1}}?api-version=7.4 {"key_ops":["sign"],"tags":{"purpose":"signing only"}} -> 200, key_ops ["sign"], the tag
        //   POST   /keys/tcae-key/{{version-1}}/wrapkey?api-version=7.4 {"alg":"RSA-OAEP","value":"aGVsbG8"} -> 500 IllegalStateException "... does not have ENCRYPT operation assigned." (a key operation its key_ops no longer allows)
        //   POST   /keys/tcae-key/{{version-1}}/sign?api-version=7.4 {"alg":"BOGUS","value":"<DIGEST>"} -> 400 (Spring's generic body: an algorithm Key Vault does not know)
        //   DELETE /keys/tcae-key?api-version=7.4 -> 200, with deletedDate and recoveryId https://{{request.host}}/deletedkeys/tcae-key
        //   GET    /keys/tcae-key?api-version=7.4 -> 404
        //   GET    /deletedkeys?api-version=7.4 -> 200, one entry
        //   GET    /deletedkeys/tcae-key?api-version=7.4 -> 200, with the key
        //   POST   /deletedkeys/tcae-key/recover?api-version=7.4 -> 200
        //   GET    /keys/tcae-key?api-version=7.4 -> 200
        //   POST   /keys/tcae-key/rotate?api-version=7.4 -> 200, a NEW version of the key ({{version-2}}), same parameters
        //   GET    /keys/tcae-key?api-version=7.4 -> 200, the rotated version is now the latest
        spec.it("updates a key's operations, refuses what they no longer allow, and deletes and recovers it") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("restricts_deletes_and_recovers_a_key")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-key/create?${V}", "{\"kty\":\"RSA\",\"key_size\":2048,\"key_ops\":[\"sign\",\"verify\",\"encrypt\",\"decrypt\",\"wrapKey\",\"unwrapKey\"]}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "create: ${b}")
            v1 = version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid"))
            st, b = kv("PATCH", "/keys/tcae-key/${v1}?${V}", "{\"key_ops\":[\"sign\"],\"tags\":{\"purpose\":\"signing only\"}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "update: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"key_ops\":[\"sign\"]", "only sign is left")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"purpose\":\"signing only\"", "the tag")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-key/${v1}/wrapkey?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"RSA-OAEP\",\"value\":\"${PLAINTEXT}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "wrap with a key that may only sign: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "does not have ENCRYPT operation assigned.", "not allowed")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-key/${v1}/sign?${V}", "{\"alg\":\"BOGUS\",\"value\":\"${DIGEST}\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an unknown algorithm: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/keys/tcae-key?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/deletedkeys/tcae-key\"", "recoveryId")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys/tcae-key?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a deleted key is not found: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/deletedkeys?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "deleted list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/keys/tcae-key\"", "listed as deleted")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/deletedkeys/tcae-key?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get a deleted key: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/deletedkeys/tcae-key/recover?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "recover: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys/tcae-key?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "it is back: ${b}")
            pause()
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-key/rotate?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "rotate: ${b}")
            v2 = version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid"))
            spec.assert_true(!same(v2, v1), "a new version")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys/tcae-key?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get the latest: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(same(version_of(jstr(b, "key.kid")), v2), "the rotated version is the latest")
            finish(rec)
        }

        // PORTING (name tcae-cert; 1 s pause between the two creates):
        //   POST   /certificates/tcae-cert/create?api-version=7.4
        //          {"policy":{"issuer":{"name":"Self"},"key_props":{"exportable":true,"kty":"RSA","key_size":2048,"reuse_key":false},"secret_props":{"contentType":"application/x-pkcs12"},"x509_props":{"subject":"CN=example.com","validity_months":12,"ekus":["1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1"],"key_usage":["digitalSignature"]}}}
        //          -> 202 {"cancellation_requested":false,"csr":"CERTIFICATE-REQUEST","id":"https://{{request.host}}/certificates/tcae-cert/pending","issuer":{..,"name":"Self"},"request_id":"{{version-1}}","status":"completed",..,"target":"https://{{request.host}}/certificates/tcae-cert"}
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert/pending?api-version=7.4 -> 200, status "completed" (Lowkey issues at once)
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert?api-version=7.4 -> 200, "cer":"CERTIFICATE-DER", "id":".../tcae-cert/{{version-1}}", "kid":"https://{{request.host}}/keys/tcae-cert/{{version-1}}", "sid":".../secrets/tcae-cert/{{version-1}}", "x5t", policy
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert/versions?api-version=7.4 -> 200, one entry
        //   POST   /certificates/tcae-cert/create?api-version=7.4 (same body) -> 202, a second version ({{version-2}})
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert/{{version-1}}?api-version=7.4 -> 200
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert?api-version=7.4 -> 200, the second version is now the latest
        //   GET    /certificates?api-version=7.4 -> 200, tcae-cert
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert/policy?api-version=7.4 -> 200, the policy: subject CN=example.com, validity_months 12, key_props, key_usage ["digitalSignature"], ekus ["1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1"], a default AutoRenew action at 80%
        //   DELETE /certificates/tcae-cert?api-version=7.4 -> 200, the bundle with deletedDate and recoveryId https://{{request.host}}/deletedcertificates/tcae-cert
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert?api-version=7.4 -> 404
        //   GET    /deletedcertificates?api-version=7.4 -> 200, one entry
        //   POST   /deletedcertificates/tcae-cert/recover?api-version=7.4 -> 200
        //   GET    /certificates/tcae-cert?api-version=7.4 -> 200
        //   DELETE /deletedcertificates/tcae-cert?api-version=7.4 -> 500 "cannot be purged" (after another delete)
        // The policy names ONE key usage and ONE extended key usage on purpose:
        // when a policy leaves them out, Lowkey Vault fills in two of each from
        // a set and returns them in a different order every run, which would
        // make the tape differ between records.
        // (A managed certificate also appears in /keys and /secrets as "managed":true
        // entries: the case does not read them, their private key material varies.)
        spec.it("creates a self-signed certificate, versions it, deletes and recovers it") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("creates_versions_deletes_and_recovers_a_certificate")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            body = "{\"policy\":{\"issuer\":{\"name\":\"Self\"},\"key_props\":{\"exportable\":true,\"kty\":\"RSA\",\"key_size\":2048,\"reuse_key\":false},\"secret_props\":{\"contentType\":\"application/x-pkcs12\"},\"x509_props\":{\"subject\":\"CN=example.com\",\"validity_months\":12,\"ekus\":[\"1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1\"],\"key_usage\":[\"digitalSignature\"]}}}"
            st, b = kv("POST", "/certificates/tcae-cert/create?${V}", body)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 202, "create: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"status\":\"completed\"", "issued at once")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert/pending?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "the pending operation: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"status\":\"completed\"", "completed")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"name\":\"Self\"", "the self issuer")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get: ${b}")
            v1 = version_of(jstr(b, "id"))
            spec.assert_true(string.length(v1) > 0, "a version")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"subject\":\"CN=example.com\"", "the subject")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert/versions?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "versions of a one-version certificate: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(same(version_of(jstr(b, "value.0.id")), v1), "its only version")
            pause()
            st, b = kv("POST", "/certificates/tcae-cert/create?${V}", body)
            spec.assert_eq(st, 202, "create a second version: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert/${v1}?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get the first version: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(same(version_of(jstr(b, "id")), v1), "the first version")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "get the latest: ${b}")
            spec.assert_true(!same(version_of(jstr(b, "id")), v1), "the second version is the latest")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/certificates/tcae-cert\"", "tcae-cert")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert/policy?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "policy: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"validity_months\":12", "12 months")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"key_size\":2048", "a 2048-bit key")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/certificates/tcae-cert?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/deletedcertificates/tcae-cert\"", "recoveryId")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a deleted certificate is not found: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/deletedcertificates?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "deleted list: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "/certificates/tcae-cert\"", "listed as deleted")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/deletedcertificates/tcae-cert/recover?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "recover: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-cert?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "it is back: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/certificates/tcae-cert?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 200, "delete again: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("DELETE", "/deletedcertificates/tcae-cert?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "purge is refused: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "The selected elements cannot be purged.", "cannot be purged")
            finish(rec)
        }

        // PORTING: the representative errors (all logged in; the 401 is in
        // the login case).
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-nope?api-version=7.4      -> 404 {"error":{"code":"com.github.nagyesta.lowkeyvault.service.exception.NotFoundException","message":"Key not found: secret:https://{{request.host}}/tcae-nope/--"}}
        //   GET   /keys/tcae-nope?api-version=7.4         -> 404 (... key:...)
        //   GET   /certificates/tcae-nope?api-version=7.4 -> 404 (... certificate:...)
        //   PATCH /secrets/tcae-nope/tcae-no-such-version?api-version=7.4 {"tags":{}} -> 500, generic (a version that is not a 32-hex id; a well-formed unknown one gives 404, but it cannot be taped: a hex version in a path is normalized to a token)
        //   PUT   /secrets/tcae-bad?api-version=7.4 {}    -> 400, Spring's generic body {"timestamp":"2000-01-01T00:00:00.000Z","status":400,"error":"Bad Request","path":"/secrets/tcae-bad"}
        //   POST  /keys/tcae-bad/create?api-version=7.4 {"kty":"BOGUS"} -> 400, generic
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-x?api-version=1.0         -> 400, generic (an api-version the emulator does not serve)
        //   GET   /secrets/tcae-x                         -> 400, generic (no api-version)
        //   POST  /secrets/tcae-x?api-version=7.4         -> 405, generic; the Allow header (a set, in varying order) is left out
        //   PUT   /secrets/tcae_bad_name?api-version=7.4 {"value":"x"} -> 500, generic (a name Key Vault does not allow: only letters, digits and dashes)
        spec.it("answers the representative error statuses") callback {
            rec, ok = begin("answers_the_representative_error_statuses")
            if ok == 0 { return }
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-nope?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a missing secret: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "NotFoundException", "not found")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Key not found: secret:", "a secret")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/keys/tcae-nope?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a missing key: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Key not found: key:", "a key")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/certificates/tcae-nope?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 404, "a missing certificate: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "Key not found: certificate:", "a certificate")
            st, b = kv("PATCH", "/secrets/tcae-nope/tcae-no-such-version?${V}", "{\"tags\":{}}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "update a malformed version: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("PUT", "/secrets/tcae-bad?${V}", "{}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "a secret without a value: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"Bad Request\"", "a generic bad request")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/keys/tcae-bad/create?${V}", "{\"kty\":\"BOGUS\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an unknown key type: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-x?api-version=1.0", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "an api-version it does not serve: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("GET", "/secrets/tcae-x", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 400, "no api-version: ${b}")
            st, b = kv("POST", "/secrets/tcae-x?${V}", "")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 405, "a method the endpoint does not take: ${b}")
            spec.assert_contains(b, "\"error\":\"Method Not Allowed\"", "method not allowed")
            st, b = kv("PUT", "/secrets/tcae_bad_name?${V}", "{\"value\":\"x\"}")
            spec.assert_eq(st, 500, "a name Key Vault does not allow: ${b}")
            finish(rec)
        }
    }

    return spec.run_summary(fw)
}
